{:edb/db-before-t 907 :edb/db-after-t 908 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534220 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:55:53.420Z" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198105 1074 "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\land B) = \\neg A \\lor \\neg B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is prime and $y$ divides $12$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is prime and }y\\text{ divides }12) & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime}∧y\\text{ divides }12) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime})∨¬(y\\text{ divides }12) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}∨y\\text{ does not divide }12 \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }y\\text{ does not divide }12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198105 1074 "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\land B) = \\neg A \\lor \\neg B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is prime and $y$ divides $12$\" is\n\n$$\n¬(xis prime andydivides12) \\mid ≡¬(xis prime∧ydivides12); ≡¬(xis prime)∨¬(ydivides12); ≡xis not prime∨ydoes not divide12; ≡xis not primeorydoes not divide12\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198113 1071 "$\\qquad$ $x$ is greater than $4$, or $x$ is irrational.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x)$: $x$ is greater than $4$\n- $Q(x)$: $x$ is rational" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198113 1071 "$\\qquad$ $x$ is greater than $4,$ or $x$ is irrational.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is greater than $4$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is rational" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198113 1074 "The sentence\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is irrational\n\ncan be expressed in symbolic form as $\\lnot Q$.\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n$P\\lor \\lnot Q$." 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198113 1074 "The sentence\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is irrational\n\ncan be expressed in symbolic form as $\\lnot Q.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\nP\\lor \\lnot Q.\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198114 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\lor B) = \\neg A \\land \\neg B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is a multiple of $5$ or $y$ divides $24$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of [math]5[/math] or }y\\text{ divides }24) & ≡¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of }5∨y\\text{ divides }24) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of }5)∧¬(y\\text{ divides }24) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not a multiple of }5∧y\\text{ does not divide }24 \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not a multiple of }5\\text{ and }y\\text{ does not divide }24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198114 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\lor B) = \\neg A \\land \\neg B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is a multiple of $5$ or $y$ divides $24$\" is\n\n$$\n¬(xis a multiple of [math]5[/math] orydivides24) \\mid ≡¬(xis a multiple of5∨ydivides24); ≡¬(xis a multiple of5)∧¬(ydivides24); ≡xis not a multiple of5∧ydoes not divide24; ≡xis not a multiple of5andydoes not divide24\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198256 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414636 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198256 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414637 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198256 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414638 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198256 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414642 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198257 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414639 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198257 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414641 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198258 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414635 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198258 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414640 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198518 1050 420.0 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198696 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194802 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198696 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414634 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198696 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198696 1071 "$\\,$ $x$ is not both positive and an integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is integer" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198696 1071 "$x$ is not both positive and an integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x)$: $x$ is positive\n- $Q(x)$: $x$ is integer" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198696 1074 "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is both positive and an integer.\n\nThe sentence above can be expressed symbolically as $P∧Q,$ and we can negate this sentence using the symbol \"$¬$\".\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as  \n\n$$\n¬(P∧Q).\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194997 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195000 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195003 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414623 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414628 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414630 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1071 "$\\,$ $a$ is even or $b$ is odd.\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186198727 1071 "$a$ is even or $b$ is odd.\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186198727 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$a$ is even or $b$ is odd\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a\\text{ is even or }b\\text{ is odd }) & ≡¬(a\\text{ is even }∨b\\text{ is odd }) \\\\  & ≡¬(a\\text{ is even })∧¬(b\\text{ is odd }) \\\\  & ≡a\\text{ is odd }∧b\\text{ is even } \\\\  & ≡a\\text{ is odd and }b\\text{ is even}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186199524 1064 "Logical operations with predicates generalize the corresponding operations on statements. As a result, all the properties of these operations are held.\n\nIn particular, for predicates $P(x_1,x_2\\ldots,x_n)$ and $Q(y_1,y_2\\ldots,y_m)$, De Morgan's laws state the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}¬(P∧Q) & ≡¬P∨¬Q \\\\ ¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬P∧¬Q\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThese can be used to negate open sentences containing conjunctions and disjunctions. For example, let's negate the following:\n\n$$\nn \\ge 0 \\:\\textbf{or}\\: 2 \\mid m\n$$\n\nApplying De Morgan's law for disjunctions, we obtain\n\n$$\n¬(n \\ge 0or2∣m) \\mid ≡¬(n \\ge 0∨2∣m); ≡¬(n \\ge 0)∧¬(2∣m); ≡n < 0∧2∤m; ≡n < 0and2∤m\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 false] [17592186199524 1064 "Logical operations with predicates generalize the corresponding operations on statements. As a result, all the properties of these operations are held.\n\nIn particular, for predicates $P(x_1,x_2\\ldots,x_n)$ and $Q(y_1,y_2\\ldots,y_m),$ De Morgan's laws state the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q) & ≡¬P∨¬Q \\\\ ¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬P∧¬Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese can be used to negate open sentences containing conjunctions and disjunctions. For example, let's negate the following:\n\n$$\nn \\ge 0 \\:\\textbf{ or }\\: 2 \\mid m\n$$\n\nApplying De Morgan's law for disjunctions, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(n\\ge 0\\,\\text{ or }\\,2∣m) & ≡¬(n\\ge 0∨2∣m) \\\\  & ≡¬(n\\ge 0)∧¬(2∣m) \\\\  & ≡n<0∧2∤m \\\\  & ≡n<0\\,\\text{ and }\\,2∤m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414558 1080 "$x$ is  irrational" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414558 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414558 1083 #uuid "007619ec-c913-5404-99ab-9ca7e135cb88" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414559 1080 "or" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414559 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414559 1083 #uuid "0962aef9-6f95-5510-8c07-1b18f3bc8236" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414560 1080 "¬P∧Q" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414560 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414560 1083 #uuid "09946243-c028-5e7f-8b25-514f9c2e0d6d" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414561 1080 "¬Y∨¬Z" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414561 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414561 1083 #uuid "0dd55b5a-0ce9-56da-98e7-46a8c78ba018" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414562 1080 "a>-1" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414562 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414562 1083 #uuid "17b670e3-459d-5123-a31a-c706894eaa35" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414563 1080 "Y∨Z" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414563 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414563 1083 #uuid "19a32f64-e897-5ff0-bfbe-9b03678c932e" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414564 1080 "$y$ is  irrational" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414564 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414564 1083 #uuid "1b44f959-eafb-5fb0-8cf3-b67b16dc0e7b" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414565 1080 "$a$ is even" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414565 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414565 1083 #uuid "273807ad-7593-517a-8539-d792e0490d5f" 13194139534220 17592186045417 true] [17592186414566 1080 "a=0" 1319